&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verve has created a more efficient and privacy-focused way to buy and monetize advertising. Verve is an ecosystem of demand and supply technologies fusing data, media, and technology together to deliver results and growth to both advertisers and publishers–no matter the screen or location, no matter who, what, or where a customer is. With offices across the globe and with an eye on servicing forward-thinking advertising customers, Verve’s solutions are trusted by more than 90 of the United States’ top 100 advertisers, 4,000 publishers globally, and the world’s top demand-side platforms. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://verve.com/&quot;&gt;verve.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are currently seeking a Senior Product Manager to own our Identity Graph / Enrichment &amp;amp; Audience Enhancement products. You will lead an already established Identity &amp;amp; Audience team to grow Verve&#39;s presence in the AdTech space through the innovative execution of key strategic initiatives. The successful candidate will participate in the development of the product strategy and product roadmaps, leading product initiatives end-to-end from ideation to launch and go-to-market. They will inform product requirements, collaborate with engineering on implementation, take products to market through extensive A/B testing &amp;amp; experimentation, and be responsible for commercial success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow our Identity Graph / Enrichment &amp;amp; Audience Enhancement products&#39; impact based on the data-driven insights that shape your roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the product increments we build are aligned with the overall strategy and product vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and lead product development end-to-end from discovery to launch to iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Come up with hypotheses, run experiments, and holdout tests to quantify the incremental value of identity and audience features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate daily with engineering, data, and product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep building the knowledge of the market landscape, including the needs of publishers, advertisers, and DSPs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle communication with internal/external stakeholders &amp;amp; partners&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand and map out cross-product dependencies with the other business units&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and monitor product KPIs to make sure the initiatives are driving product &amp;amp; business success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience in product management roles, at least 2+ years of product management experience in the AdTech industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem solver - You can capture business problems, come up with solutions, and write good product requirement documents to keep everyone aligned on the scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technically skilled - You have a good understanding of databases, data structures, and how software systems can be integrated and exchange data with each other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter &amp;amp; self-motivator - you don’t wait to be told what needs to be done; you take full ownership of product initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborator &amp;amp; communicator - you can gather tech and business stakeholders across functions &amp;amp; levels around you to work towards a common goal, speaking their language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achiever - You focus on outcomes &amp;amp; prefer to have something done rather than have it perfect; you value an iterative process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven - you value the power of data and can perform data analysis to make decisions / assess results based on metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Just a few of the benefits waiting for you at Verve:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recharge with 3 &lt;strong&gt;Wellness Days &lt;/strong&gt;throughout the year, in addition to your annual vacation and public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support your mental well-being with our &lt;strong&gt;Workplace Mental Health Solution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Boost your professional knowledge with our annual &lt;strong&gt;training budget &amp;amp; internal webinars&lt;/strong&gt;, and level up your language skills through our &lt;strong&gt;German/English classes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen team connections while exploring new cultures through our monthly &lt;strong&gt;Work&amp;amp;Travel raffle,&lt;/strong&gt; offering a chance to work from one of our global offices (after 2 years of employment)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;… and even more reasons to join us!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Verve provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you are a California resident subject to the California Consumer Privacy Act, &lt;a href=&quot;https://verve.com/california-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to understand how Verve processes your personal information and how you can exercise your rights.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;If you are located in the EU or UK visit our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot; href=&quot;https://verve.com/applicant-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;privacy policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt; to understand how Verve processes your personal information and how you can exercise your rights.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Ledgy, we’re on a mission to make Europe a powerhouse of entrepreneurship by building a modern, tech-driven equity management and financial reporting platform for private and public companies. In 2026, we aim to be the leading provider for European IPOs and reporting for share-based payments. We are a value-based company with a core focus on being humble, transparent, ambitious and impactful, all in order to delivery the best experience for our customers and end users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to partner with some of the world’s leading investors. New Enterprise Associates led our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://techcrunch.com/2022/09/21/ledgy-a-carta-for-european-startups-to-manage-equity-and-cap-tables-raises-22m-from-nea-sequoia-and-more/&quot;&gt;$22m Series B&lt;/a&gt; round in 2022, with Philip Chopin joining Sequoia’s Luciana Lixandru on our board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We were founded in Switzerland in 2017 and today we operate globally from offices in Zurich and London. We encourage diversity and are an international team coming from 26 different countries and speaking 25 different languages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior DevOps Engineer at Ledgy, you&#39;ll build the infrastructure and tooling that help our engineers ship quickly and reliably. You&#39;ll join our Platform team, collaborating with engineers and InfoSec to improve CI/CD, observability, and cloud infrastructure for a product that helps companies manage equity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our challenge is to make delivery faster, production easier to operate, and AI-assisted development safer - while keeping complexity and costs in check.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; We hire remotely across Spain, Germany, Poland, and Romania.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team you&#39;ll join:&lt;/strong&gt; Platform - Builds the infrastructure and tooling that help our engineers ship quickly and reliably, working with InfoSec to improve CI/CD, observability, and cloud infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Work On&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud infrastructure.&lt;/strong&gt; Evolve our GCP and Kubernetes cloud architecture and setup with Terraform, improving reliability, simplicity, and cost visibility and enabling scaling to multiple availability regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CI/CD and developer experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Speed up feedback loops, reduce flaky builds, and turn recurring support requests into self-service tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability.&lt;/strong&gt; Reduce alert noise, define meaningful SLOs, and make production issues easier to diagnose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security and automation.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with InfoSec on secure delivery, access controls, and guardrails for AI-assisted workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll also join our incident-response on-call rotation during working hours and help prevent recurring issues. As we expand our servicing of public companies and jurisdictions, this on-call might evolve to compensated 24h/7 hour rotation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll Thrive in This Role If You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don&#39;t worry if you don&#39;t tick every box. These are the things that would make you an especially good fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong DevOps / SRE background designing and operating cloud infrastructure and production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked with Kubernetes and infrastructure as code, ideally GCP and Terraform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy building fast, reliable CI/CD pipelines and improving developer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can diagnose issues across networking, infrastructure, and application code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write maintainable code and bring a practical approach to observability and security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Value collaboration, mentorship, and thoughtful trade-offs between reliability, complexity, and cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are curious about supporting AI-assisted development safely - no AI specialism required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with Node.js, MongoDB or Temporal is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech Stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work in TypeScript: React, Tailwind CSS, and tRPC on the front end, and tRPC, Node.js, MongoDB, and Temporal on the back end. Infrastructure runs on GCP, Terraform Cloud, Kubernetes, Docker, and GitHub Actions. For observability and incident response we use Grafana, Sentry, and PagerDuty.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t need to know all of it. We don&#39;t expect proficiency in every part of this stack. Strong infrastructure fundamentals and the ability to learn matter more than knowing every tool already.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Your Journey Could Look Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 30 days:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get to know Ledgy, the Platform team, and our internal users with an onboarding buddy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore our infrastructure and delivery workflows, and ship your first improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze current state of our cloud infrastructure and propose meaningful enhancements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 3 months:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently deliver improvements to CI/CD, observability, or infrastructure design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share operational ownership and help reduce recurring friction for engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to architecture discussions and document what others need to operate our systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 6-12 months:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own DevOps and SRE function and DevOps initiatives from problem definition through rollout and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver measurable improvements to developer experience, reliability, or cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape our platform&#39;s direction and mentor other engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The interview process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting to know you (45 min):&lt;/strong&gt; Meet with someone from our people team to talk about your experience and to ask questions about the role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live Coding (60 min):&lt;/strong&gt; An equity domain problem to solve collaboratively using your preferred language and IDE. We want to see how you think, so this step does not allow AI. But you can freely look up syntax questions if you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Design (60 min):&lt;/strong&gt; A system design session where you will design an architecture for a problem from the Ledgy domain using a visual tool of your choice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DDSA (45 min):&lt;/strong&gt; A Deep Dive into real System Architecture that you have built, owned and monitored.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture Interview:&lt;/strong&gt; A chance to meet one of our founders and your hiring manager for a 30-minute chat about Ledgy&#39;s mission and values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offer&lt;/strong&gt; 🎉&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Being part of Ledgy means&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recharge and re-energize with flexible working hours, 25 days of vacation, and up to 40 days of remote work from outside your home country.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We make space for your own professional development, with a generous yearly learning &amp;amp; development budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will receive a competitive salary + benefits + equity. All salaries are aligned with competitively benchmarked ranges based on work location and levelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Per the EU Pay Transparency Directive, the pay range for this role is listed below for all legally required countries. Pay within the range reflects your skills, experience and the scope of the role, and is set using objective criteria applied consistently across the team. Certain roles are also eligible for additional rewards including variable pay under the applicable plan. Ledgy offers equity through our employee option plan. Benefits offered vary by country and type of employment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Spain pay range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€79.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€97.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verve has created a more efficient and privacy-focused way to buy and monetize advertising. Verve is an ecosystem of demand and supply technologies fusing data, media, and technology together to deliver results and growth to both advertisers and publishers–no matter the screen or location, no matter who, what, or where a customer is. With offices across the globe and with an eye on servicing forward-thinking advertising customers, Verve’s solutions are trusted by more than 90 of the United States’ top 100 advertisers, 4,000 publishers globally, and the world’s top demand-side platforms. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://verve.com/&quot;&gt;verve.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are currently seeking a Senior Product Manager to own our Identity Graph / Enrichment &amp;amp; Audience Enhancement products. You will lead an already established Identity &amp;amp; Audience team to grow Verve&#39;s presence in the AdTech space through the innovative execution of key strategic initiatives. The successful candidate will participate in the development of the product strategy and product roadmaps, leading product initiatives end-to-end from ideation to launch and go-to-market. They will inform product requirements, collaborate with engineering on implementation, take products to market through extensive A/B testing &amp;amp; experimentation, and be responsible for commercial success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow our Identity Graph / Enrichment &amp;amp; Audience Enhancement products&#39; impact based on the data-driven insights that shape your roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the product increments we build are aligned with the overall strategy and product vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and lead product development end-to-end from discovery to launch to iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Come up with hypotheses, run experiments, and holdout tests to quantify the incremental value of identity and audience features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate daily with engineering, data, and product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep building the knowledge of the market landscape, including the needs of publishers, advertisers, and DSPs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle communication with internal/external stakeholders &amp;amp; partners&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand and map out cross-product dependencies with the other business units&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and monitor product KPIs to make sure the initiatives are driving product &amp;amp; business success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience in product management roles, at least 2+ years of product management experience in the AdTech industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem solver - You can capture business problems, come up with solutions, and write good product requirement documents to keep everyone aligned on the scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technically skilled - You have a good understanding of databases, data structures, and how software systems can be integrated and exchange data with each other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter &amp;amp; self-motivator - you don’t wait to be told what needs to be done; you take full ownership of product initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborator &amp;amp; communicator - you can gather tech and business stakeholders across functions &amp;amp; levels around you to work towards a common goal, speaking their language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achiever - You focus on outcomes &amp;amp; prefer to have something done rather than have it perfect; you value an iterative process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven - you value the power of data and can perform data analysis to make decisions / assess results based on metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Just a few of the benefits waiting for you at Verve:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recharge with 3 &lt;strong&gt;Wellness Days &lt;/strong&gt;throughout the year, in addition to your annual vacation and public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support your mental well-being with our &lt;strong&gt;Workplace Mental Health Solution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Boost your professional knowledge with our annual &lt;strong&gt;training budget &amp;amp; internal webinars&lt;/strong&gt;, and level up your language skills through our &lt;strong&gt;German/English classes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen team connections while exploring new cultures through our monthly &lt;strong&gt;Work&amp;amp;Travel raffle,&lt;/strong&gt; offering a chance to work from one of our global offices (after 2 years of employment)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;… and even more reasons to join us!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Verve provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you are a California resident subject to the California Consumer Privacy Act, &lt;a href=&quot;https://verve.com/california-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to understand how Verve processes your personal information and how you can exercise your rights.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;If you are located in the EU or UK visit our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot; href=&quot;https://verve.com/applicant-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;privacy policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt; to understand how Verve processes your personal information and how you can exercise your rights.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Mechatronic System Architect | Medical Robotics (m/f/d)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Maastricht, Aachen, and Eindhoven region, working mainly on-site with our development partner in Maastricht. Regular travel to Hamburg and to clinical sites, about 2 to 4 days per month.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; CTO&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the venture: ROB&#39;E&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ROB&#39;E is a Hamburg-based medtech startup and part of the NLC Health Ventures portfolio. We are developing a robotic system that holds and steers a standard transesophageal echocardiography (TEE) probe during structural heart interventions. Interventionalists get stable, reproducible echo views, and echocardiographers no longer have to stand next to the patient in the X-ray field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our first-generation prototype has been used in a first-in-human study with published results. We are now developing the next generation from scratch as a fully compliant medical device for CE marking and FDA clearance. The team includes a CTO, a System Software Architect and a Head of Quality &amp;amp; Regulatory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are the mechatronic design authority of ROB&#39;E. You own the system architecture, the hardware requirements and the technical decisions for the mechanics, drives, sensing and electronics of our robot. You work on site with our engineering development partner in the Maastricht area and steer their team on our behalf. This is a hands-on senior role: you design yourself, review the work of others and make sure the hardware is safe, verifiable and ready for design transfer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the mechatronic system architecture: robotic device, drives, force and torque sensing, real-time controllers, safety supervisor, power supply and the interface to commercial TEE probes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate user and system requirements into subsystem and interface specifications and keep them traceable through verification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as technical counterpart to our engineering development partner, from ideation, technology and part selection through design reviews and approval of design outputs. Challenge cost and effort and make the make-or-buy call per subsystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the System Software Architect on the hardware/software split, real-time control, and safety architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the hardware contribution to risk management (ISO 14971), including design FMEA and risk control measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and lead hardware verification, pre-compliance and full compliance testing for electrical safety and EMC (IEC 60601-1, IEC 60601-1-2) with external test houses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute hardware documentation to the design history file and technical documentation under our ISO 13485 quality system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build prototypes for verification, usability studies and clinical evaluation, together with suppliers and the development partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for cost and manufacturability from the start and prepare the transfer to series production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MSc or PhD in mechatronics, mechanical, electrical or systems engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 8 years of hardware development experience, including at least 3 years as a system architect or lead engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on development of active medical devices through design controls, from concept to verified design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with IEC 60601-1, IEC 60601-1-2 and ISO 14971, and working knowledge of ISO 13485 and MDR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in motion systems: drives, transmissions, encoders, force/torque sensing and motion safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience steering external engineering partners or suppliers, including technical reviews and cost control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English and comfortable working in a small, fast moving startup team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with medical robotics, catheter or endoscope handling, or image guided intervention systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of cleanable and reprocessable device design and single use interface components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dutch or German language skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A key role in a clinically validated medtech venture, with real influence on the product and the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close collaboration with interventional cardiologists and direct exposure to the cath lab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Permanent employment with a competitive salary and an employee stock option plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A lean, senior team with short decision paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;1pw1999&quot; data-start=&quot;3755&quot; data-end=&quot;3777&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;3758&quot; data-end=&quot;3777&quot;&gt;Why Join ROB’E?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;3778&quot; data-end=&quot;4091&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;tdwgj1&quot; data-start=&quot;3778&quot; data-end=&quot;3847&quot;&gt;Build a &lt;strong data-start=&quot;3788&quot; data-end=&quot;3825&quot;&gt;category-defining MedTech company&lt;/strong&gt; from an early stage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1wf7lvs&quot; data-start=&quot;3848&quot; data-end=&quot;3901&quot;&gt;Work directly with experienced physician-founders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1tgz6th&quot; data-start=&quot;3902&quot; data-end=&quot;3967&quot;&gt;Take ownership across strategy, product, and company building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We would love to hear from exceptional individuals who are excited about building a company at the intersection of AI, robotics, and cardiovascular medicine.&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics is a leading global sports platform redefining how fans connect with the teams, players and moments they love. Our businesses — Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, Fanatics Events, Fanatics Advertising, Fanatics Markets and Fanatics Studios — maximize the presence and reach for hundreds of partners globally and create a one-stop experience that allows fans to buy, bet, collect, and earn, while engaging with sports in deeper, more immersive ways. This includes licensed fan gear and lifestyle products, sportsbook and iGaming, physical and digital trading cards, live events, premium sports entertainment content, credit card offerings and more. Together, they form a powerful, integrated ecosystem — connected by the Fanatics ONE loyalty program and FanCash, the currency of sport — delivering personalized experiences to over 100 million fans worldwide. Fanatics holds partnerships with over 900 sports properties, from professional leagues and players’ associations to teams, colleges and retail partners; over 7,000 athletes and celebrities; and over 2,000 retail locations, including all Lids stores. Backed by a team of more than 22,000 employees, Fanatics is committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Markets is the real-money prediction and trading app where you can invest in moments you care about. Built on a secure platform, we let users predict real-world outcomes and trade on events they actually follow—from sports and entertainment to political elections and beyond. Our mission is to redefine how fans engage with the moments and markets that matter most. We&#39;re looking for the right people to help us build the future of prediction markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer within our Platform team, you will help define the technical direction of the platform underpinning our exchange and trading systems. You will lead the design and evolution of our infrastructure and platform standards to support a highly available, low-latency exchange, partnering closely with exchange engineers and engineering leads to enable rapid innovation without compromising stability or security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a balance of deep hands-on software engineering, systems thinking and technical leadership. You will lead complex projects that support the exchange—from load-testing environments and mock integrations to monitoring and automated recovery. You will turn ambiguous requirements into practical designs, own delivery from ideation to production and help operate the platform as the exchange goes live. The balance of coding and infrastructure work varies by project, but you should be comfortable independently developing new software as well as improving existing systems, setting platform standards and mentoring engineers across experience levels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On the engineering side, we are pioneering the use of AI as a code collaborator. We need engineers who have moved beyond experimentation—who actively use tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or GitHub Copilot to ship production code faster while maintaining exceptional quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and development of software tools, services and automation that solve complex infrastructure, reliability and developer experience challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve the architecture of highly available cloud-native infrastructure, balancing performance, reliability, security and cost as the platform grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction for CI/CD pipelines and developer tooling, remaining hands-on in delivering improvements to the software delivery lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development of load-testing environments and supporting software, including mock services and integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and evolve standards for AI-augmented development, using effective prompting and validation practices to increase velocity without sacrificing code quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and mitigate AI-generated code pitfalls, such as security vulnerabilities or over-abstraction, and help teams evaluate the impact on quality and productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the design and implementation of platform security safeguards and compliance standards to protect the integrity of the firm’s systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the system observability roadmap and lead improvements to monitoring, tracing, alerting and automated recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with exchange, product and engineering leads to resolve architectural trade-offs, align priorities and deliver scalable platform solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers across experience levels, lead technical design discussions and raise engineering standards across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the on-call rotation, lead incident response for team-owned services and drive engineering improvements that prevent recurring incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in software, backend or platform engineering, with a track record of leading complex technical projects and delivering production software and scalable, cloud-native environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep software development expertise, including the ability to independently design, build, test and deploy services or substantial tools from scratch and guide others through complex implementation decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on Kubernetes experience, including designing and operating production environments, troubleshooting complex failures, and establishing patterns for high availability and efficient scaling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on experience with AWS and infrastructure as code using Terraform, including making architectural decisions across complex environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High proficiency in Java and Python; Go is a plus. You should be comfortable bridging the gap between infrastructure and application logic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of distributed systems and the ability to make and explain trade-offs between low latency, high availability, scalability and operational complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping CI/CD and observability approaches, with hands-on knowledge of tools such as Prometheus, Grafana or Datadog.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in using AI collaborators such as Claude Code, Cursor or GitHub Copilot to ship production code and improve engineering workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to evaluate AI-generated code for security gaps or architectural errors and establish rigorous testing and validation practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to turn ambiguous problems into a clear technical direction and deliver improvements across team boundaries, balancing immediate needs with long-term architectural health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, including the ability to explain complex technical decisions, influence without formal authority and collaborate effectively with distributed engineering and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring senior engineers and building alignment around technical standards and architectural decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in high-growth startup environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with financial systems, exchanges, real-money transactions or regulatory compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in designing and building internal developer platforms, tools, CLI applications or infrastructure automation services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing load-testing environments, mock services or automated recovery systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading technical initiatives spanning multiple teams or evolving platform architecture through significant growth or change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the role, your interview and onboarding experience may include in-person components, such as onsite interviews or Launching into Better: LIVE—a multi-day cultural immersion in New York City for full-time, non-seasonal hires. These sessions are designed to build connection and bring our culture to life, though specific travel and participation requirements will be confirmed based on your role and location. Your recruiter will provide clear guidance at each stage of the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to build the future of sports betting? If you possess some of these skills but not all of them, we still encourage you to apply! Please note that &lt;strong&gt;visa sponsorship is not available&lt;/strong&gt; for this position. We are open to &lt;strong&gt;fully remote candidates based in the United Kingdom.&lt;/strong&gt; Remote employees may also be eligible for a home office setup stipend.&lt;/p&gt;
